$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Amide Compounds II. General
Procedure C. To a flame-dried flask were added the carboxylic acid (1.0
equiv), dicyclohexylcarbodiimide (1.1 equiv), dimethylaminopyridine (1.1
equiv), dodecylamine (1.0 equiv), and CH2Cl2 (0.40 M). After stirring at
room temperature for 24 h, the reaction mixture was filtered through a
Celite plug and concentrated. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography. 4-amino-2-trifluoromethylpyridine-C4-3-bromophenoxyhybrid
(S56): Prepared from 4- amino-2-trifluoromethylpyridine and S36 1 using
general procedure C to furnish S56 in a 4.0% yield. HRMS (ESI-TOF)
calculated for C16H15BrF3N2O2 [M+H]+: m/z 403.0269, found 403.0259; 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.60 (d, J = 5.5 Hz, 1H), 7.87 (d, J = 2.0 Hz,
1H), 7.70-7.57 (m, 2H), 7.14 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (dt, J = 8.0, 1.4
Hz, 1H), 7.03 (t, J = 2.1 Hz, 1H), 6.80 (ddd, J = 8.1, 2.5, 1.0 Hz, 1H),
4.05 (t, J = 5.8 Hz, 2H), 2.65 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 2.27- 2.18 (m, 2H);
13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.3, 159.2, 151.1, 149.9-148.7 (m), 146.0,
130.7, 124.5-118.0 (m), 124.2, 122.9, 117.7, 115.3, 113.3, 110.4-110.2
(m), 66.7, 34.0, 24.4.
